<h1>Research Overview and Past Projects</h1>


<h2>Context and Motivation</h2>
<p>
  Thin particles structures refer to systems (material structures, particles, crack-like voids) where one characteristic length is much smaller than the other(s). Such structure typically arises in electromagnetism (strong field enhancement by thin nanoparticles, in photonic crystals made of periodic assembling of nano-rods, or metasurfaces with disordered dielectric rods).
</p>
<p>
  It is fundamental to understand how the near-field is affected by a thin particle, as well as understanding how the coupling effects caused by several ones (number and sizes) contribute to field enhancement.
</p>

